{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1527093-requiem-for-rome-2e-fast-casting","id":1527093,"title":"Requiem for Rome 2e: Fast Casting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-19T16:20:30-08:00","id":1527093,"title":"Requiem for Rome 2e: Fast Casting","content":"The Requiem for Rome 2e book on the ST Vault introduces &quot;Fast Casting&quot;, which lets blood sorcerers cast a ritual instantly by taking on certain conditions.<br /> <br /> For Theban Sorcery, it makes sense how this works: you spend the willpower, the sacrament disintegrates, and the ritual takes effect. But for Cr\u00faac (and Veneficium and Necromancy and anything else that takes vitae to activate), do you need to take several turns to spend the vitae? For example, a Blood Potency 1 Augur fast-casting a level 5 ritual would still need five turns to spill the five vitae required?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T00:26:20-08:00","id":1527108,"title":"","content":"Presumably. The general rule in CofD games is that if you can't fuel a power during one turn, you do it over several and take the action during the turn where you spent the last required fuel point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T17:56:49-08:00","id":1530228,"title":"","content":"Of note, though, is that I believe you can take other actions on those preparatory turns while reflexively spending the required vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T13:27:45-08:00","id":1530399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1527093-requiem-for-rome-2e-fast-casting#post1527093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Requiem for Rome 2e book on the ST Vault introduces &quot;Fast Casting&quot;, which lets blood sorcerers cast a ritual instantly by taking on certain conditions.<br /> <br /> For Theban Sorcery, it makes sense how this works: you spend the willpower, the sacrament disintegrates, and the ritual takes effect. But for Cr\u00faac (and Veneficium and Necromancy and anything else that takes vitae to activate), do you need to take several turns to spend the vitae? For example, a Blood Potency 1 Augur fast-casting a level 5 ritual would still need five turns to spill the five vitae required?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Cruac and the Veneficium are kind of exceptional because you actually have to physically spill blood after you spend the first point. That's mostly a narrative conceit, and you could just say that you're &quot;expelling&quot; the blood at the rate of your Blood Potency. At any rate, assuming we're just treating it like normal Vitae expenditures, like other Disciplines, if you can't do it all in one turn, you can spend previous turns spending it reflexively until you hit the requirement.<br /> <br /> That said, Vitae for Cruac/the Veneficium can come from other vampires, so you could also potentially fast cast by having your coven toss a bunch of blood in the sacrificial bowl and just let 'er rip in a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}